Ashley has a credit card with the following conditions:

\begin{itemize}
\item There is no interest-free period.
\item Interest is charged at the end of each month at $18.25\%$ per annum, compounding daily, from the purchase date (included) to the last day of the month (included).
\end{itemize}

Ashley’s credit card statement for April is shown, with some figures missing.

\exfigure{5832_q27_1}

The minimum payment is calculated as $2\%$ of the closing balance on 30 April.

Calculate the minimum payment.

Harrison has a credit card with no interest free period and an interest rate of $18.25\%$ p.a. compounded daily. Interest is charged on the date of purchase but not the date the account is paid. Harrison had paid his credit card off in full before the end of June and makes the following purchase during the month of June.

\extable{496_q23_t1}

Harrison pays his credit card bill in full on the 4th of July. How much interest does he pay?

